{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-52413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/75a7f3bfae55a97fbc0c05e2e0356d21de6ceabcc82ac3e1c965838a636f5ecc.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-52413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider the line $y=3x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 3x+1.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-52413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a65358a8b5ef7055c4952abcc1fce216480695a123f917818b4365ffd9c265f4"} {"question" "q-52413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-52413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y<2\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\le 2\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 3x+1 \\\\ y\\le 2\\end{aligned}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-52413" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2\\end{aligned}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/387709ca72b5591528b5f5ac95886f0dab331ef2cb67955803e7a252cecef966.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=2x+3.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le 2x+3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines our shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ y\\le 2x+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a65358a8b5ef7055c4952abcc1fce216480695a123f917818b4365ffd9c265f4"} {"question" "q-90319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y<\\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ y\\ge 2x+3\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y>\\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ y<2x+3\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ y\\ge 2x+3\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ y\\le 2x+3\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ y\\le 2x+3\\end{aligned}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ y\\le 2x+3\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90174" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the diagrams shows the solution of the following system?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 2x \\\\ y\\le -2x\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90174" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To graph the first inequality $y\\le 2x,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=2x.$\n\n- Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, the line itself is included in the solution, so the line is solid.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* or equal to those on the line, so we shade *below* the line.\n\nTo graph the second inequality $y\\le -2x,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=-2x.$ \n\n- Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, the line itself is included in the solution, so the line is solid.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* or equal to those on the line, so we shade *below* the line.\n\nThe intersection of the solutions is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/438928da5e9de5e9ba3d2abbe06b6f1f8b6b0598a0b82bec1f51824b9ef72a71.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3