e.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-52462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider the line $y=3x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<3x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=1.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y<3x+2 \\\\ y<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-52462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a65358a8b5ef7055c4952abcc1fce216480695a123f917818b4365ffd9c265f4"} {"question" "q-52462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-52462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y<3x+2 \\\\ y<1\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y<3x+2 \\\\ y>1\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y>3x+2 \\\\ y<1\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y>3x+2 \\\\ y>1\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 3x+2 \\\\ y\\le 1\