e-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-x+3.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\"  inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>-x+3,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+y>3.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=2x.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict.  Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>2x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y>2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90054" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a65358a8b5ef7055c4952abcc1fce216480695a123f917818b4365ffd9c265f4"} {"question" "q-90054" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90054" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x+y<3 \\\\ y<2x\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x+y<3 \\\\ y>2x\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y<2x\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y>2x\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x+y\\le 3 \\\\ y\\ge 2x\\end{aligned}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90054" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y>2x\\end{aligned}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-110093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/f03b04087cde111d9db2b9e499a0d700105b7150496cc6c117c0f2e2b05e74c2.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-110093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider the line $y=x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $3x+2y=-6.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{3}{2}x-3.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le -\\frac{3}{2}x-3,\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n3x+2y\\le -6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y<x+2 \\\\ 3x+2y\\le -6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-110093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a65358a8b5ef7055c4952abcc1fce216480695a123f917818b4365ffd9c265f4"} {"question" "q-110093" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-110093" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y<x+2 \\\\ 3x+2y\\ge -6\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y<x+2 \\\\ 3x+2y\\le -6\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y>x+2 \\\\ 3x+2y\\ge -6\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge x+2 \\\\ 3x+2y>-6\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ 3x+2y>-6\\end{aligned}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-110093" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}y<x+2 \\\\ 3x+2y\\le -6\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-110078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/3905dacc3977857933a48ced329fc245b357f732aec520e67998efc0b5d7cdab.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-110078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider the line $x+2y=-8.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x-4.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x-4,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+2y\\ge -8.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge -8 \\\\ y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-110078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a65358a8b5ef7055c4952abcc1fce216480695a123f917818b4365ffd9c265f4"} {"question" "q-110078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/matha