 \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>2x.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $x-4y=-8.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{4}+2.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le \\frac{x}{4}+2,\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx-4y\\ge -8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y>2x \\\\ x-4y\\ge -8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a65358a8b5ef7055c4952abcc1fce216480695a123f917818b4365ffd9c265f4"} {"question" "q-90171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y<2x \\\\ x-4y\\ge -8\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y<2x \\\\ x-4y\\le -8\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y>2x \\\\ x-4y\\ge -8\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y>2x \\\\ x-4y\\le -8\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 2x \\\\ x-4y<-8\\end{aligned}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}y>2x \\\\ x-4y\\ge -8\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/4b3487492c235ddeaa46d6b64cc3cc908e02bacf061ab84474401c9d6e3ce634.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider the line $x+2y=2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+1.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x+1,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+2y\\ge 2.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=2x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le 2x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge 2 \\\\ y\\le 2x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90053" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a65358a8b5ef7055c4952abcc1fce216480695a123f917818b4365ffd9c265f4"} {"question" "q-90053" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90053" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y>2 \\\\ y>2x+1\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge 2 \\\\ y\\ge 2x+1\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge 2 \\\\ y\\le 2x+1\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\le 2 \\\\ y\\ge 2x+1\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\le 2 \\\\ y\\le 2x+1\\end{aligned}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "q-90053" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge 2 \\\\ y\\le 2x+1\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f52905f69ca98169e3e7006f25135a2fc71e6ea64c85d5f5f04bfca92ce119b"} {"question" "e-1056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/bdb5279236cdc7671efa0f309b0a07d5ffc131f9d3c33a048f286fdef4588fcd.png)\n\nWhich system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/example-1056.json" "file_sha256" "0bbe4cf5f81fee178baff665dbd4ca0449a44896f5686106b6e6509f6401e907"} {"question" "e-1056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider the line $y = 2x - 1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\leq 2x - 1.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y = -x+2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\geq -x + 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines our shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 2x-1 \\\\ y\\ge -x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/example-1056.json" "file_sha256" "0bbe4cf5f81fee178baff665dbd4ca0449a44896f5686106b6e6509f6401e907"} {"question" "e-7959" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/c9209c8978b86043b5d57d4a357a480a0209914598a0d7f2a810539cc050c473.png)\n\nWhich system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/example-7959.json" "file_sha256" "e9d47668f25339650b46a5c70fad402d90a3a48fdb5bbd04afc988511a1f378b"} {"question" "e-7959" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider the line $y=2x-3.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\gt 2x - 3.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y = x + 1.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\lt x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y>2x-3 \\\\ y<x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/example-7959.json" "file_sha256" "e9d47668f25339650b46a5c70fad402d90a3a48fdb5bbd04afc988511a1f378b"} {"question" "e-7960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/69a4b7d160f9a3990034f7e9170cc20d90eba33bd87397f8436836fdd5520e84.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities represents the shaded region shown in the graph above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/example-7960.json" "file_sha256" "5dac7c5f07cf08d9b1d792112ce17dc37c06f85e68ceaeea858d382649b40009"} {"question" "e-7960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider the line $y = \\dfrac{1}{3}x+3.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\leq \\dfrac{1}{3}x+3.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y = x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\lt x+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\le \\frac{1}{3}x+3 \\\\ y<x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/example-7960.json" "file_sha256" "5dac7c5f07cf08d9b1d792112ce17dc37c06f85e68ceaeea858d382649b40009"} {"question" "e-7964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/e92ea6fc292a771333cc12b9554b58bd4ba5f358195982c5ac3fd6bd2a9d06ff.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/example-7964.json" "file_sha256" "0c3d1a321897508596408abb15bcd675319e076eb60bca724aff108f50a57a45"} {"question" "e-7964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider the line $y=1.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is \n\n$$\ny < 1.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $x - y = 2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny =x- 2.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\geq  x - 2,\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx-y \\leq 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y<1 \\\\ x-y\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/example-7964.json" "file_sha256" "0c3d1a321897508596408abb15bcd675319e076eb60bca724aff108f50a57a45"}] "usage" {"e-7960" [] "e-7964" [] "q-90171" [] "e-1056" [] "e-7959" []} "basis" 1077 "retractions" [[17592186111346 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1535/Source/Images/q-90171.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?"] [17592186110216 :question/problem "Which system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1535/Source/Images/3edbb889f6978133fc2ae041a3085a33.png)"] [17592186110216 :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y = 2x - 1$. Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\leq 2x - 1\n$$\n\nNow consider the line\n\n$$\ny = -x+2\n$$\n\nSince the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\geq -x + 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines our shaded region is\n\n$$\n{y \\le 2x - 1; y \\ge - x + 2\n$$"] [17592186110461 :question/problem "Which system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1535/Source/Images/344928c0eea99cd3497661d8845d95b4.png)"] [17592186110461 :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=2x-3$. Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n$y \\gt 2x - 3$.\n\nNow consider the line\n\n$$\ny = x + 1\n$$\n\nSince the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n$y \\lt x+1$.\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n${y > 2x - 3; y < x + 1$."] [17592186110462 :question/problem "Which of the following systems of inequalities represents the shaded region shown in the graph above?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1535/Source/Images/457d1898a5945703bd6b2621ffa8f08a.png)"] [17592186110462 :question/worked-solution "Consider the line\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{1}{3}x+3\n$$\n\nSince the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\leq \\dfrac{1}{3}x+3\n$$\n\nNow consider the line\n\n$$\ny = x+2\n$$\n\nSince the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n$y \\lt x+2$.\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{y \\le \\frac{1}{3}x + 3; y < x + 2\n$$"] [17592186110463 :question/problem "What system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1535/Source/Images/8d691714edd32c1331cb1041545ed34e.png)"] [17592186110463 :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=1$. Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n$y < 1$.\n\nNow consider the line $x - y = 2$. Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n$y =x- 2$.\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\geq x - 2\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx-y \\leq 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{y < 1; x - y \\le 2\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186110172 17592186110173 17592186110174 17592186110175 17592186110176] "immutable_fields" [[17592186110171 :answer-field/correct] [17592186110171 :answer-field/id] [17592186110171 :answer-field/key] [17592186110171 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
